see "../src/harness.vox".

(D2 - a campaign whose scratch root cannot be written must abort loudly,
 not report "findings: 0". Provenance: a run whose cwd was deleted under
 it sailed to completion through 2,817 getcwd errors, compiled nothing,
 and reported success on top of total failure. Here we make the scratch
 root read-only (mkdir + chmod 555) and run a tiny campaign through
 'run shell', capturing the exit code and combined stdout+stderr. The run
 must exit non-zero and must NOT print the line "findings: 0". Cleanup is
 UNCONDITIONAL - a failed run must not leave ./vf_scratch read-only for
 the next test - so the chmod 755 + rm -rf runs regardless of how the
 assertions came out. 'run shell' of chmod/mkdir is harness setup, not a
 generated program, so the signal-vs-exit distinction rule does not
 apply here.)

a number called 'the clean before' is 'run shell' of "rm -rf ./vf_scratch ./vf_uw_findings ./vf_uw_out" and 5000.
a number called 'the ro dir' is 'run shell' of "mkdir ./vf_scratch && chmod 555 ./vf_scratch" and 5000.
a number called 'the run exit' is 'run shell' of "./build/vox-fuzz gen --count 2 --seed 1 --out ./vf_uw_findings > ./vf_uw_out 2>&1" and 30000.
a number called 'the findings grep' is 'run shell' of "grep -q -x 'findings: 0' ./vf_uw_out" and 5000.
Print "scratch abort exit non-zero: {'the run exit' is not 0}".
Print "no findings: 0 in output: {'the findings grep' is not 0}".
a number called 'the cleanup' is 'run shell' of "chmod 755 ./vf_scratch 2>/dev/null; rm -rf ./vf_scratch ./vf_uw_findings ./vf_uw_out" and 5000.